    "summary": "High‑energy ’72 with blazing Other One sequence and stellar China>Rider",
    "blurb": "The Palace Theater show delivers a high‑energy second set highlighted by the legendary Cryptical Envelopment → Drums → The Other One → Wharf Rat suite and a seamless China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue. Jerry’s flanged leads, Phil’s front‑forward bass bombs, and Keith’s early keyboard texture make this September ’72 performance a standout among the run.",
    "review": "The Palace Theater on September 23, 1972 finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. After a solid first set that opens with a rollicking \"Big River\" and weaves through classics like \"Sugaree\" and \"Bird Song,\" the band really kicks into high gear in the second half. The Cryptical Envelopment → Drums → The Other One → Wharf Rat marathon showcases Jerry’s on‑fire guitar, complete with flanger‑laced leads that cut through the warm SBD mix, while Phil drops bass bombs that drive the improvisation forward. Keith Godchaux adds a bright early‑’70s keyboard sheen that perfectly complements the soaring vocals of Donna Jean and Bob. The seamless transition from \"China Cat Sunflower\" into \"I Know You Rider\" remains one of the set’s most electric moments, and the closing medley of \"Sugar Magnolia\" through \"One More Saturday Night\" keeps the momentum blazing to the final encore.",
